# Example fixture: magnetite (Fe3O4), rhombohedral primitive cell (14 atoms),
# built from its space group (Fd-3m, No. 227) via pymatgen's
# Structure.from_spacegroup, with Fe at 8a/16d (no free parameter) and O at
# 32e with oxygen positional parameter u=0.379 (origin choice 2; a = 8.396
# Ang). Verified physically sensible after generation: min Fe-O = 1.76 Ang,
# min O-O = 2.87 Ang, min Fe-Fe = 2.97 Ang -- all in the expected range for
# an oxide spinel. Approximate/illustrative values (not re-verified against
# a primary crystallographic reference) -- fine for exercising code paths,
# don't use for production DFT without checking a proper source first.
#
# An earlier version of this fixture used u=0.2548, which put two O atoms
# only 0.11 Ang apart (unphysical) -- caught by stb-crystalbuilder's
# overlap sanity check when regenerating this same structure from scratch.
#
# Chosen specifically because Fe sits on *two* symmetrically distinct sites
# (tetrahedral 8a-type and octahedral 16d-type in the conventional cell,
# labeled 'a'/'d' in this primitive setting) while O is a single site -- the
# textbook example of "same element, different Wyckoff class". Used to
# exercise stb-defect's --all-inequivalent-sites (expect 2 Fe sites found,
# multiplicities 2 and 4; 1 O site, multiplicity 8). Fe positions/order are
# unchanged from the earlier version, so site indices in stb-defect's
# test.sh (site #1 and #5) still refer to the same two Fe sites.

NumberOfSpecies    2
NumberofAtoms      14

%block ChemicalSpeciesLabel
 1   26   Fe
 2   8   O
%endblock ChemicalSpeciesLabel

LatticeConstant 1.0 Ang

AtomicCoordinatesFormat  Fractional

%block LatticeVectors
 0.00000000   4.19800000   4.19800000
 4.19800000   0.00000000   4.19800000
 4.19800000   4.19800000   0.00000000
%endblock LatticeVectors

%block AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
  0.12500000   0.62500000   0.12500000   1
  0.62500000   0.12500000   0.12500000   1
  0.12500000   0.12500000   0.62500000   1
  0.12500000   0.12500000   0.12500000   1
  0.50000000   0.50000000   0.50000000   1
  0.75000000   0.75000000   0.75000000   1
  0.37900000   0.86300000   0.37900000   2
  0.38700000   0.87100000   0.87100000   2
  0.37900000   0.37900000   0.86300000   2
  0.87100000   0.38700000   0.87100000   2
  0.37900000   0.37900000   0.37900000   2
  0.87100000   0.87100000   0.87100000   2
  0.86300000   0.37900000   0.37900000   2
  0.87100000   0.87100000   0.38700000   2
%endblock AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
